Compilation Stages in C 

****** What is compilation?
Compilation is the process of converting human-written C code into machine-executable code through multiple steps.




****** Stages of Compilation
file.c
  ↓ Preprocessor(gcc -E file.c -o file.i)
file.i
  ↓ Compiler(gcc -S file.i -o file.s)
file.s
  ↓ Assembler(gcc -c file.s -o file.o)
file.o
  ↓ Linker(gcc file.o -o output)
Executable (ELF)
  ↓ Loader
Program runs → main()


**********Loader (when running the executable)

The Loader:

Reads ELF executable
Loads program into memory (text, data, bss)
Loads shared libraries (libc.so.6, etc.)
Fixes addresses & relocations
Passes control to _start → then main()


******Who call main()?Need execution order?

OS Loader → _start → __libc_start_main() → main() → exit()




